{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The AsciiDoc syntax offers several approaches for preventing substitutions from being applied."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To prevent a punctuation character from being interpreted as an attribute reference or formatting syntax (e.g., _, ^) in normal content, prepend the character with a backslash ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "\\"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ")."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": "ex-backslash",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In /items/\\{id}, the id attribute isn't replaced.\nThe curly braces around it are preserved.\n\n\\*Stars* isn't displayed as bold text.\nThe asterisks around it are preserved.\n\n\\&sect; appears as an entity reference.\nIt's not converted into the section symbol (&sect;).\n\n\\=> The backslash prevents the equals sign followed by a greater\nthan sign from combining to form a double arrow character (=>).\n\n\\[[Word]] is not interpreted as an anchor.\nThe double brackets around it are preserved.\n\n[\\[[Word]]] is not interpreted as a bibliography anchor.\nThe triple brackets around it are preserved.\n\nThe URL \\https://example.org isn't converted into an active link."
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Prevent unintended substitutions with a backslash in normal content"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The backslash can also prevent character replacements, macros, and attribute replacements. The results of "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Example 1"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "#ex-backslash"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " are below."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "In /items/{id}, the id attribute isn’t replaced. The curly braces around it are preserved."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "*Stars* isn’t displayed as bold text. The asterisks around it are preserved."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "&sect; appears as an entity reference. It’s not converted into the section symbol (§)."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "=> The backslash prevents the equals sign followed by a greater than sign from combining to form a double arrow character (⇒)."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "[[Word]] is not interpreted as an anchor. The double brackets around it are preserved."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "[[[Word]]] is not interpreted as a bibliography anchor. The triple brackets around it are preserved."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The URL https://example.org isn’t converted into an active link."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Notice that the backslash is removed so it doesn’t display in your output."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To prevent two adjacent characters (e.g., __, ##), from being interpreted as AsciiDoc syntax you need to precede it with two backslashes ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "\\\\"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ")."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": "ex-double-slash",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The text \\\\__func__ will appear with two underscores\nin front of it and after it.\nIt won't be italicized."
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Prevent unintended substitutions with two backslashes in normal content"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The results of "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Example 2"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "#ex-double-slash"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " are below."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The text __func__ will appear with two underscores in front of it and after it. It won’t be italicized."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_escape_with_backslashes",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Escape with backslashes"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A passthrough is the primary mechanism by which to escape content in AsciiDoc. They’re far more comprehensive and consistent than using a backslash. As the name implies, a passthrough passes content directly through to the output document without applying any substitutions."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can control and prevent substitutions in inline text with the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "inline passthrough macros"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "pass:pass-macro.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and for entire blocks of content with the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "block passthrough"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "pass:pass-block.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_passthroughs",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Passthroughs"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Escape and Prevent Substitutions"
      }
    ]
  }
}
